# /etc/default/soleur-doppler-token — re-deliverable web-host credential (#7095)
#
# THE FILENAME IS LOAD-BEARING. infra_config_classify_files (infra-config-gate.sh:46-62)
# derives a dest's class from basename(dest): for dest /etc/default/soleur-doppler-token it
# looks for <infra_dir>/soleur-doppler-token or <infra_dir>/soleur-doppler-token.tmpl.
# Renaming this file to anything else classes the dest `missing` =>
# content_gate_repo_file_missing => rc=1 => the whole apply reds and the token never lands.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (#7095, 2026-07-30). web-1's boot-baked Doppler service token in
# /etc/default/webhook-deploy was revoked at 11:19:30.614Z. That file is written EXACTLY ONCE,
# at first boot, by cloud-init.yml (`printf ... > /etc/default/webhook-deploy`) from
# var.doppler_token. It has no Terraform resource, no replace_triggered_by, and no drift
# detector — so a rotation silently bricks the deploy path plus five other units, with a host
# replace impossible (cx33, orderable in 0 of 3 EU DCs). Measured onset: container-restart-monitor
# +18.17s after the mint, inngest-heartbeat and cron-egress-resolve +26.14s, zero failures in the
# preceding 53h.
#
# This file is the RE-DELIVERABLE sibling: it rides the infra-config webhook channel
# (push-infra-config.sh -> /hooks/infra-config -> infra-config-apply.sh FILE_MAP ->
# infra-config-install.sh DEST_SPEC), the same path that delivers ci-deploy.sh, and it is
# registered in deploy_pipeline_fix's triggers_replace hash. A change to the rendered content
# therefore re-fires the push on the next apply.
#
# ADDITIVE, NEVER A REWRITE OF THE ORIGINAL. Consumers pick this up by systemd later-wins
# (an EnvironmentFile= line placed AFTER the original) or by an explicit guarded shell source.
# /etc/default/webhook-deploy and /etc/default/inngest-server are deliberately left in place:
# inngest-bootstrap.sh:616-617 fail-closes the host if DOPPLER_PROJECT goes missing from the
# latter, and per Sharp Edge 7 a host replace is not available as a recovery.
#
# NO DOPPLER_CONFIG_DIR HERE, DELIBERATELY (#6536). /etc/default/webhook-deploy carries
# DOPPLER_CONFIG_DIR=/tmp/.doppler; importing it into units that run as a different user
# re-opens the ownership-clash surface. Units that need it still get it from the original file.
#
# SHAPE IS ENFORCED IN THREE PLACES, because a malformed render here bricks every unit that
# sources it and the remediation channel is one of them:
#   1. variable "doppler_token" validation (variables.tf) — fails at `terraform plan`, before a
#      byte reaches the host. This is the only layer that is provably non-bricking.
#   2. infra-config-install.sh rejects an /etc/default/* payload whose non-blank lines are not
#      all KEY=VALUE (reject "envfile_shape") — refuse-to-install beats install-and-brick.
#   3. systemd-analyze verify runs before infra-config-apply.sh schedules its self-restart.
# Note EnvironmentFile=- covers ABSENT and UNREADABLE, but NOT empty-valued: a bare
# `DOPPLER_TOKEN=` would win by later-wins and silently blank a good credential. Layer 1 is
# what closes that.
DOPPLER_TOKEN=${doppler_token}
# Sentry ingest parameters, baked (#7095 R3). ci-deploy.sh hydrates these FROM DOPPLER using
# the very token that is dead in this failure mode, and every Sentry emitter is guarded on all
# three being non-empty — so under a revoked token the host emits ZERO Sentry events. That is
# why 341 unit failures over 5.7h produced no page, and it silently collapsed the two-vendor
# independence story to one vendor. Baking them here makes the paging route survive exactly the
# fault class it exists to report. These are public DSN components (already shipped in the
# client bundle), so this adds no new exposure class. Exact precedent: server.tf bakes
# BETTERSTACK_INGEST_URL into /etc/default/web-private-nic-guard for the same reason.
SENTRY_INGEST_DOMAIN=${sentry_ingest_domain}
SENTRY_PROJECT_ID=${sentry_project_id}
SENTRY_PUBLIC_KEY=${sentry_public_key}
